<title>BELGIUM: Clarke says EMU stability deal just out of reach.</title>
<headline>Clarke says EMU stability deal just out of reach.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-12-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>British Chancellor of the Exchequer Kenneth Clarke said on Monday evening that European union finance ministers had been quite close to a deal on a stability pact on fiscal discipline, but could not clinch it.</p>
<p>&quot;We were quite close to an agreement, but we were not quite able to reach it,&quot; he told reporters after the talks in Brussels broke up around 2045 GMT.</p>
<p>Earlier, diplomats said talks had broken up without a deal being reached on the fiscal discipline plan, adding that ministers would meet again next week to try to thrash out a deal. -- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6800</p>
